@startuml sd-amqp-event-propagation
skinparam style strictuml
autonumber
title SD - Criar rota: comando CQRS + propagação do evento pelo RabbitMQ

actor "Backoffice" as User
participant "RouteController\n(instância 1)" as Ctrl
participant "RouteService" as Svc
participant "RouteRepository\n(escrita)" as RR
participant "RouteProjector" as Proj
participant "RouteReadRepository\n(leitura)" as RM
participant "ReplicationOutbox" as Outbox
participant "AmqpReplicationPublisher" as Pub
participant "airports.events\n(fanout)" as Ex
participant "ReplicationEventConsumer\n(instância 2)" as Cons2
participant "IdempotencyGuard\n(inbox)" as Inbox
participant "RouteService\n(instância 2)" as Svc2

User -> Ctrl : POST /api/routes
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Svc : createRoute(dto, isReplication=false)
activate Svc
note right of Svc : UMA transação:\nescrita + leitura + outbox
Svc -> RR : save(route)
Svc -> Proj : project(route)
Proj -> RM : save(RouteReadModel)
Svc -> Outbox : enqueue(evento)
Outbox -> Outbox : grava ReplicationTask (PENDING)
Svc --> Ctrl : RouteViewDTO
Ctrl --> User : 201 Created
deactivate Svc
deactivate Ctrl
note right of User : O cliente não espera pelo broker.

== Em segundo plano (de 2 em 2 s) ==
Pub -> Pub : lê as tarefas PENDING
Pub -> Ex : publica ROUTE_CREATED\n(messageId = eventId, UUID)
Ex --> Pub : confirmação do broker
Pub -> Pub : tarefa = DONE
note right of Pub : Sem confirmação -> tenta mais tarde.\n10 falhas -> FAILED.

== O broker entrega uma cópia a cada fila ==
Ex -> Cons2 : fila airports.events.airports-routes-2
activate Cons2
Cons2 -> Cons2 : evento meu? -> ignora
Cons2 -> Inbox : runOnce(eventId)
activate Inbox
Inbox -> Inbox : já processado? -> ignora
Inbox -> Svc2 : createRoute(dto, isReplication=true)
activate Svc2
Svc2 -> Svc2 : grava escrita + leitura\n(last-writer-wins)
Svc2 --> Inbox : ok
deactivate Svc2
Inbox -> Inbox : grava processed_event\n(na mesma transação)
Inbox --> Cons2 : ack
deactivate Inbox
deactivate Cons2
note right of Cons2 : Erro -> 3 tentativas -> DLQ.
note over Ex : O Flight Operations recebe o mesmo evento\nna sua própria fila.
@enduml
